[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    146[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Row 27 evidence
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    147[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    148[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `err26_27_duplicate_hit_temp_key_asymmetry` inserts 4000 string keys, then for
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    149[0m:[38;5;10m[49m each key poisons `table->temp_key` with a sentinel and re-puts the key. If
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    150[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `temp_key` still holds the sentinel afterwards, the duplicate was found by the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    151[0m:[38;5;10m[49m wrap-around sub-loop (which does **not** write `temp_key`); otherwise by the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    152[0m:[38;5;10m[49m upper sub-loop (which does). The test asserts both libraries classify every one
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    153[0m:[38;5;10m[49m of the 4000 keys identically, and that both classes are non-empty — so the C's
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    154[0m:[38;5;10m[49m asymmetry is genuinely exercised, not merely assumed.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    155[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    156[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Row 56 refinement
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    157[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    158[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `512 << (block >> 1)` on x86-64 at `-O0` compiles to a variable `shl`, whose
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    159[0m:[38;5;10m[49m count is taken mod 64. `block == 110/111` ⇒ shift 55 ⇒ `2^64` wraps to
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    160[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `blocksize == 0`, so the oversized-block branch is taken for any length —
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    161[0m:[38;5;10m[49m testable, and tested. `block == 128` ⇒ shift `64 & 63 == 0` ⇒ `blocksize == 512`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    162[0m:[38;5;10m[49m again. Values such as `block == 200` (shift `100 & 63 == 36` ⇒ `blocksize == 2^45`)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    163[0m:[38;5;10m[49m make the C request 32 TiB from `realloc`, get `NULL`, and write through it: that
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    164[0m:[38;5;10m[49m is row 4's OOM crash and is excluded from the test, identically for both
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    165[0m:[38;5;10m[49m libraries.
