[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    190[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## What "outputs match byte-for-byte" means here
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    191[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    192[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `stbds_hmput_key` & friends return a heap pointer, and the two libraries get
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    193[0m:[38;5;10m[49m different `malloc` addresses, so raw pointer values are not comparable. What the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    194[0m:[38;5;10m[49m tests compare after **every single call** (`tests/common/mod.rs::Dual::check`) is:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    195[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    196[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `stbds_array_header`: `length`, `capacity`, `temp`;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    197[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * the whole `stbds_hash_index`: `slot_count`, `slot_count_log2`, `used_count`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    198[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `used_count_threshold`, `used_count_shrink_threshold`, `tombstone_count`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    199[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `tombstone_count_threshold`, `seed`, and the arena's `remaining` / `block` /
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    200[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `mode` / block-list length;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    201[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **every** `bucket.hash[j]` and `bucket.index[j]` across all `slot_count` slots;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    202[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * the element key material — copied bytes for binary / `SH_NONE` tables, the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    203[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (deliberately shared) caller pointer for `SH_DEFAULT`, the pointed-to strings
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    204[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   for `SH_STRDUP` / `SH_ARENA`;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    205[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * a per-insert payload tag stamped into `[key_end, elemsize)`, so `hmdel_key`'s
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    206[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   element `memmove` is observable;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    207[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `table->temp_key`, once a string-mode put has initialised it.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    208[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    209[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `stbds_make_hash_index` never initialises `stbds_hash_index::temp_key`, in the C
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    210[0m:[38;5;10m[49m or in the Rust, and `hmdel_key` swaps in a freshly `realloc`'d index on
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    211[0m:[38;5;10m[49m shrink/rebuild, so `temp_key` is only compared while it is defined.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    212[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    213[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `row75`/`row75b` are the strongest layout checks: a table built by one library is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    214[0m:[38;5;10m[49m inserted into, queried, and deleted from by the *other* library. That can only
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    215[0m:[38;5;10m[49m work if the header, hash index, bucket layout, hash functions and probe sequence
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    216[0m:[38;5;10m[49m are bit-identical.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    217[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    218[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Combinations deliberately excluded, and why
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    219[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    220[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Two `(string.mode, mode)` families are excluded from `row76`. In both the C
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    221[0m:[38;5;10m[49m itself leaves defined behaviour, identically for both libraries, so there is no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    222[0m:[38;5;10m[49m comparable observable:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    223[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    224[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **`SH_NONE` + `mode >= 1`.** The `switch` default arm `memcpy`s the key
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    225[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   *bytes* into the element, but `stbds_is_key_equal` then evaluates
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    226[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `strcmp(key, *(char **)elem)` — it reads those bytes back as a pointer. The
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    227[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   first lookup of an already-present key dereferences a fabricated pointer and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    228[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   segfaults. The insert-only half of this configuration is row 37 and *is*
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    229[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   tested.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    230[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **`mode == 2` combined with a delete that relocates the final element.**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    231[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `hmdel_key` gates the string re-find on `mode == STBDS_HM_STRING` exactly, so
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    232[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   with `mode == 2` it re-finds the moved element in *binary* form while the slot
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    233[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   was hashed as a string. The re-find fails and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    234[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `STBDS_ASSERT(slot >= 0)` calls `abort()`. `mode == 2` is therefore covered by
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    235[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   row 32 (inserts + lookups) and row 58 (deletes restricted to the final
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    236[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   element, where that branch is skipped), plus
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    237[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `errors::err46_mode_two_skips_strdup_free`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    238[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    239[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `stbds_arrfreef(NULL)`, `stbds_hash_string(NULL, …)` and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    240[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `stbds_strreset(NULL)` are missing null checks in the C that terminate the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    241[0m:[38;5;10m[49m process; see the "Not-testable rows" section of `ERRORS.md`.
